  "body": "When generating text, models compute raw scores called logits for every vocabulary token. A softmax function turns these logits into probabilities that sum to one across all choices.\n\n[[visual:1]]\n\nApplying top-k filtering keeps only the $k$ highest scoring tokens and sets the rest to zero probability. Because the valid probabilities must sum to one again for sampling, the remaining scores are divided by their combined sum in a step called renormalization.\n\nThis division increases the relative probability assigned to each surviving token compared to the original full distribution. Consequently, the reported probability of the chosen token changes because it is scaled up by the inverse of the kept share.",
